  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't build or run it here, so how it looks and how fast it runs are untested.\n\nThe scene is a night harbor. It has a dark sky with 420 emissive stars, bloom, a custom GLSL water plane, and a dark shoreline with hills, houses with a few lit windows, a pier with a lamp, and five boats.\n\nRockets launch from the shore at irregular intervals. Each rises with a trail of glowing dots, then bursts into a spherical shell of about 170 sparks, with an optional smaller inner shell in a second color. Sparks slow down, fall under gravity and shrink as they fade. About half the bursts leave trailing streaks. The first three bursts are gold, red and blue, and later ones add green and violet.\n\nSparks are drawn as instanced emissive spheres, one pool per color, updated every frame. Up to four recent bursts light the scene in three ways:\n- **Water:** reflects each burst as a shimmering streak.\n- **Sky:** a soft additive halo around the burst tints the sky.\n- **Shore:** a point light faintly lights the silhouettes.\n\nThe camera is fixed. `window.__TASK_STATE__` holds `{ bursts, activeParticles }` and updates every frame. `__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first animation frame after the engine reports ready.\n\nI tuned the light intensities and shader constants from the numbers alone, so the glow and silhouette levels may need adjusting once it's viewed.",
